    "result_text": "All 14 tests pass, build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the registration-date behavior for `POST /api/owners` in this Spring PetClinic REST app. When no `registrationDate` is supplied it defaults to the server's current date, and it's returned in ISO `YYYY-MM-DD` format (a supplied date is preserved).\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an optional `registrationDate` property (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Since `Owner` composes `OwnerFields` via `allOf`, the field becomes both a create input and a read-back output. The `format: date` mapping makes the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` use `LocalDate`, which Jackson serializes as `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `LocalDate registrationDate` field (`@Column(name = \"registration_date\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n3. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 In `addOwner`, after mapping the payload, default the date when absent: `if (owner.getRegistrationDate() == null) owner.setRegistrationDate(LocalDate.now());`.\n\n4. **DB schemas** \u2014 Added a nullable `registration_date DATE` column to the `owners` table in the hsqldb (used by tests), h2, postgres, and mysql `schema.sql` files.\n\nThe MapStruct `OwnerMapper` maps the `LocalDate` field automatically by name in both directions, so no mapper change was needed.\n\nResults: `Cp07Tests` (both `coreDefaultsToToday` and `functionalityKeepsSuppliedDate`) pass, and the full suite is green \u2014 **14 tests, 0 failures, BUILD SUCCESS**.",
